"A knight's first binding is their first affixation, binding authority into a chosen skill."
"It is done so knights can fight demons in chaotic places."
"The topic is taboo among Artonans, and many swear respectful silence about it."
"Many die during the first binding or within a few years of it."
"Families often dread it; future knights may avoid attachment to a peer expected to die."
"Before choosing, a candidate consults the Contract, designers and theorists about the skill."
"A grand presentation spell previews the chosen skill in its humblest form before it is revealed."
"Most raised in the Rapports survive the first binding; those raised outside have a harder time."
"For days after a binding, knights find their skills agonizing to use."
"Some shallow wizards find knights' bound authority revolting."
"A candidate casts a last spell as an unbound wizard, witnessed by friends."
"A knight whose bound skill fails may have to bind again."
